-- title:
--   Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation family on the Hecke tower
-- statement:
--   The statement is an existence assertion for a family of uniformisation maps, one for each prime of the Hecke tower, out of an extensive interface of hypotheses. The data and hypotheses are as follows; they are grouped, and where a group is summarised the text says so.
--
--   **Primes and level.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ and a nonzero natural number $N$, with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`), $r\nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r\nmid N$ (`hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`).
--
--   **Base rings.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible $\pi\in\mathcal O$ (`hπ`) for which $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), with residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Further, a characteristic-zero domain $\mathrm{Onr}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), with $(\pi)$ maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`) and every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side.** Rationals $a,b$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`: $a>0$ or $b>0$, and the completion at a finite place $v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or above $\bar r$); a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`); `hΛℤ`, that every rational integer lies in $\Lambda$; and a map $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)\times\mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)$ with `hcoord`: it is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative in the Frobenius-twisted sense of `IsOrderCoord`, injective, has dense image modulo all powers of $r$, and computes reduced traces.
--
--   **Moduli schemes.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point-assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ making it a coarse moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ for $\Lambda$ (`h𝒳`). An auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ (`hn`) prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`); a scheme $M$ with $f_M$ and $\mathrm{ptF}$ which is a fine moduli scheme for such curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`); a group $G$ acting on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ forming a level-twist action (`hρ`); and a forgetful morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point-assignments (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner.** For every prime $\ell$ distinct from $r$ and $\bar r$, a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $g_\ell$ and $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ which is a coarse moduli scheme for curves with an extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) whose effect on points is forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and passing to an $\ell$-isogenous curve (`hd₁`); and endomorphisms $a_r$, $a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side and arithmetic groups.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) with $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$ (`hv`); the group $\Gamma_t$, characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units integral away from $v$ for $R_1$; families $s_\ell$ of quaternion units and $s_{f,\ell}$ of finite-adelic units with `hs` (four clauses: $s_{f,\ell}$ has component $s_\ell\otimes 1$ at every finite place not above $r$, component $1$ at the places above $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $s_{f,\ell}^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}$ of $\Lambda_1$ and $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$); the groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell}=\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The special fibre object and its quasi-isogenies.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/\pi$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ in two variables for $A_0$, and `hA₀` asserting that $\theta_0$ identifies the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with $\mathrm{coord}$. Endomorphism families $e,e':\Gamma_t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`he`) with degrees $\deg$, subject to the group `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here): each pair $(e_\gamma,e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; $e$ is multiplicative and sends rational scalars to scalars up to powers of $r$, and conversely an $e_\gamma$ that is an integer multiplication up to powers of $r$ forces $\gamma$ to be a rational scalar; for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$ by an element of that centraliser whose $E_0$-image is $r^{k_\gamma}g\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$; the action on the fixed full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ is given by labels in $\Lambda$ that are multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; and every $r$-power isogeny preserving the level structure on a geometric pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$.
--
--   **Eichler-order and twin-order endomorphisms.** An order $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators covering $R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) and $\hat e:R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê`), subject to `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e`, `hE5g` (summarised here: additivity for the group law, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action and level preservation; unitality, multiplicativity and agreement with the $\Lambda$-action on integers; the adjoint relation $\hat e_{\bar x}\hat e_x=[\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$; compatibility with $e_\gamma$ when $x=r^{k}\gamma$; a joint $E_0$-comparison for $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$ simultaneously; and stability of $R_2$ under the main involution). A twin maximal order $\Lambda_{1s}$ with $R_1\le\Lambda_{1s}$ and $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$ (`hΛ₁s`, `hR₁Λ₁s`, `htwin`), an order $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ with $r$-power denominators covering $\Lambda_{1s}$ and containing $R_2$ (`hR₂'`, `hR₂'o`, `hR₂'r`, `hR₂R₂'`), and $\hat e':R_2'\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê'`) subject to `hE6a`, `hE6b1`, `hE6b2`, `hE6b3`, `hE6c`, `hE6d`, `hE6e1`, `hE6e2`, `hE6f` (summarised here: the same group-law, $\Lambda$-equivariance, unitality, multiplicativity, integer and adjoint relations; $\hat e'$ extends $\hat e$; $R_2'$ is stable under the involution and $\hat e'$ is injective; and if $\hat e'_z$ kills all $q$-torsion for a prime $q\neq r$ then $r^{K}z\in q\Lambda_{1s}$ for some $K$).
--
--   **Drinfeld moduli package.** A ring map $\iota:\mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)\to\mathrm{Onr}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the reduction of $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $\mathrm{Onr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$ with `hη` (three clauses: $\eta$ identifies admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism over Noetherian bases, commutes with base change, and is locally surjective after a Zariski cover); and an injective $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action to $M_2(K_0)$ with `hE₀` (its image, scaled by a fixed power of $r$, is exactly the matrices over $\mathcal O$).
--
--   **Identification of the $G$-functor with the Deligne-datum functor.** A family $eD$ of maps from the points of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal O\,MD$ over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr}\to B$ and a Deligne datum, which is natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), has first component the structure map (`hfstD`), turns the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action into the twisted action on $\Omega$ (`hGLD`), turns $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist of the first component (`hPiD`), and for which $\pi$-translates exist (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Reduction comparison and base point.** A ring map $\kappa:\mathrm{Onr}/\pi\to\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`), and a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ on $A_0$.** A curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ and an exponent $k_w$ (with the stated compatibilities over the base) such that $a_w,a_w'$ realise the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ (`hBSw`) preserving the level structure (`hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` provides a single $g$ realising $\Gamma_t$ through $\iota_0$ and the composite $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ through $\iota_0(\bar w)$ in the $E_0$-picture.
--
--   **The rigidification-to-$G$ map.** A map $\Xi$ sending, over each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:\mathrm{Onr}\to B$, a rigidified curve to a point of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.GPoint}$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected bases its $\mathrm{Onr}$-leg is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under base change of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matched up to $r$-power comparison) and `hΞdef` (its value is computed by $\eta$ applied to a rigidified object transported through $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$ with a twist exponent $j\le 1$).
--
--   **Hecke dictionary.** An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ together with `heqΓ`, `heqW` and `heqS`: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on $\Xi$-points; an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ corresponds to $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$; and, under its own package of hypotheses (an adelic unit in the prime Hecke set at $r$, quaternion and adelic elements $s,s_f$ satisfying the four adelic clauses, an extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$, a level-$\ell$ isogeny datum $A_{0s}$, an $r$-power isogeny pair back to $A_0$ preserving the level, and a joint $E_0$-comparison through $\iota_0(\overline{s})$), a level-$\ell$ isogeny corresponds to $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\ell s^{-1})g_0^{-1}$.
--
--   **The fine-level family $\Theta_f$ and its properties.** A homomorphism $\theta_t:\Gamma_t\to G$ and a family $\Theta_f$ sending a triple (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr}\to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$, an element of $G$) to a $\pi$-nilpotent point of $f_M$, subject to `hnat` (naturality in $B$), `hG` (translating the $G$-component by $h$ corresponds to applying $\rho(h)$), `hi'` (the twisted action by $\iota_0(\gamma)$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, corresponds to multiplying the $G$-component by $\theta_t(\gamma)$), `het` (unique lifting along a surjection whose kernel multiplies to zero) and `hfib` (over algebraically closed fields, equality of values is equivalent to the existence of $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ with the prescribed relations among the $G$-components, the Deligne data and the $\mathrm{Onr}$-legs, the latter through $\mathrm{vdet}$).
--
--   **The comparison clauses.** `hC0e` and `hC0u`: existence, over connected Noetherian bases, and uniqueness of the normalised level-$n$ transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification. `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`: existence, over connected bases, of a rigidified curve with prescribed $(\psi,P)$; uniqueness of such a curve up to an isomorphism matched by an $r$-power comparison of rigidifications; and its base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps between connected Noetherian bases. `hC2` and `hC2c`: the underlying morphism of $\Theta_f$ at $G$-component $1$ is the fine moduli point of the curve with its transported level-$n$ structure, and its composite with $p$ is the coarse moduli point of the curve. `hC3`: the twisted action by $\iota_0(\gamma)$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, produces a second rigidification of the *same* curve, with the same $(\psi',P')$-normalisation, whose level-$n$ transport is the $\chi(\theta_t(\gamma))$-twist of the original and whose transported extra level-$\ell$ structures, for primes $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $B$ and extra levels on $A_0$ stabilised by $e_\gamma$, define the same subscheme condition on points. `hC4` and `hC4pi`: the corresponding statements for an action by $r^{c}g_0\iota_0(h)g_0^{-1}$ and for $\pi$-translation. `hC5`, the one-leg form: over an algebraically closed field, given two rigidified curves normalised by $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ and an isomorphism of the underlying curves, there are $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ such that the twisted action by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ carries $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$, the isomorphism carries the $\chi(\theta_t(\gamma))$-twist of the first level-$n$ transport to the second, and for each prime $\ell\neq r$ invertible in the field and each extra level on $A_0$ together with transported extra levels $C$, $C'$ on the two curves, the isomorphism matches $C$ with $C'$ if and only if $e_\gamma$ stabilises that extra level on $A_0$.
--
--   **Tower extra-level data.** For each $\ell$ away from $r$ and $\bar r$: an extra level-$\ell$ structure $C_0(\ell)$ on $A_0$, a curve $A_{0s}(\ell)$ with morphisms $a_s,a_s',b_s,b_s'$ and exponent $k_s(\ell)$ such that $a_s,a_s'$ realise the level-$\ell$ isogeny of $(A_0,C_0(\ell))$ (`hLIs`), $(b_s,b_s')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_s(\ell)}$ (`hBSs`) preserving the level (`hBSslev`), and `hJOINTs` provides a joint $E_0$-comparison realising $\Gamma_t$ through $\iota_0$ and the composite $a_s$ followed by $b_s$ through $\iota_0(\overline{s_\ell})$. Moreover `hSTAB`: $e_\gamma$ stabilises $C_0(\ell)$ precisely when $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$; and `hCLe`, `hCLu`: existence and uniqueness (as a condition on points) of the extra level-$\ell$ structure on a curve $E$ transported from a given extra level on $A_0$ along a rigidification, for primes $\ell\neq r$ invertible in the base.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above there exists a family $\Theta_T$ assigning, to each prime $\ell$ distinct from $r$ and $\bar r$, to each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, and to each pair $(\psi,P)$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:\mathrm{Onr}\to B$ and a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that the following five assertions hold.
--
--   (i) *Naturality.* For all Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B,B'$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi:B\to B'$ and every $x$, $\Theta_T(\ell)$ applied to the image of $x$ equals the image under $\varphi$ of $\Theta_T(\ell)(x)$ in the functor of $\pi$-nilpotent points of $g_\ell$.
--
--   (ii) *Value.* For all $\ell$, all Noetherian $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, all $\psi$, all Deligne data $P$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with a rigidification $\varrho$ relative to $A_0$ along $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\psi$, and every extra level-$\ell$ structure $C$ on $E$: if the $\mathrm{Onr}$-leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\psi$, if $eD(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ is carried to $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$, and if $C$ is transported from $C_0(\ell)$ in the sense that for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t'$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(B/\pi B)$ and every point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over $t'$ whose image in $E$ factors through $C$, the point $(R\text{ followed by }\varrho.\varphi)$ followed by $\varrho.g_A$ factors through $C_0(\ell)$, then the underlying morphism of $\Theta_T(\ell)(\psi,P)$ equals the underlying morphism of the coarse moduli point $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ of the pair $(E,C)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}B$.
--
--   (iii) *Compatibility with the fine-level family.* For all $\ell$, all Noetherian $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and all $x$, the morphism $\Theta_T(\ell)(x)$ followed by $d_0(\ell)$ equals the morphism $\Theta_f(x,1)$ followed by $p$.
--
--   (iv) *Invariance.* For all $\ell$, all Noetherian $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ and all $x,x'$: if $x'$ is obtained from $x$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$, then $\Theta_T(\ell)(x')=\Theta_T(\ell)(x)$.
--
--   (v) *Fibres.* For all $\ell$, every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\psi:\mathrm{Onr}\to k$ and all Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$: $\Theta_T(\ell)(\psi,P)=\Theta_T(\ell)(\psi,P')$ if and only if there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ whose twisted action by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ carries $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$.
--
--   This is the tower step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld $p$-adic uniformisation of Shimura curves attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: from the uniformisation family $\Theta_f$ on the fine level-$n$ moduli scheme it produces, for each prime $\ell$ away from $r$ and $\bar r$, the corresponding family on the coarse moduli scheme of curves with an extra level-$\ell$ structure, together with its value, degeneracy-compatibility, $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$-invariance and fibre properties. It is the form of the result used by the node that assembles the lift of the tower family over the whole Hecke tower.
